  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thig6.5" class="h1">Thig 6:5  Anopamā, the Millionaire’s Daughter</h4>
          <div class="verse">
            <p>Born in a high-ranking family</p>
            <p>with much property, great wealth,</p>
            <p>consummate in complexion &amp; figure,</p>
            <p>I was the daughter of Majjha, the treasurer.</p>
            <p>Kings’ sons sought for me,</p>
            <p>rich merchants’ sons</p>
            <p class="v2">longed for me.</p>
            <p>One of them sent my father a messenger,</p>
            <p>saying, “Give me Anopamā.</p>
            <p>I will give in return</p>
            <p class="v2">eight times her weight</p>
            <p class="v2">in jewels &amp; gold.”</p>
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>But I, having seen</p>
              <p class="v2">the One Self-awakened,</p>
              <p class="v2">unsurpassed, excelling the world,</p>
              <p>paid homage to his feet,</p>
              <p>sat down to one side.</p>
              <p>He, Gotama, from sympathy,</p>
              <p>taught me the Dhamma.</p>
              <p>And as I sat in that very seat,</p>
              <p class="v2">I attained the third fruit</p>
              <p class="v2">[of non-return.]</p>
              <p>Then I cut off my hair,</p>
              <p>and went forth into homelessness.</p>
              <p>Today is the seventh day</p>
              <p>since I made craving</p>
              <p class="v2">wither away.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
          </div><!--end verse-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
